# Component fixture

This page exercises every component in the auto-injected set. No `<script>` import
block is present; all components arrive via the MDsveX layout module seam.

## Aside

<Aside title="Note" type="note">
This is a **note** aside. Token-bound border, left-bar, and shadow.
</Aside>

<Aside title="Caution" type="caution">
This is a **caution** aside. Warn accent.
</Aside>

<Aside title="Danger" type="danger">
This is a **danger** aside. Error accent.
</Aside>

## Steps

<Steps>
<li>

**Install** — `pip install py-wyrd`

</li>
<li>

**Author** — create a `DataCard` around your data interface.

</li>
<li>

**Register** — upload the card to a running server.

</li>
</Steps>

## Tabs

<Tabs>
<Tab label="Python">

```python
from wyrd.data import DataCard
card = DataCard(name="example")
```

</Tab>
<Tab label="Rust">

```rust
let card = DataCard::new("example");
```

</Tab>
<Tab label="YAML">

```yaml
apiVersion: wyrd/v1
kind: Data
metadata:
  name: example
```

</Tab>
</Tabs>

## LangTabs / LangTab

<LangTabs>
<LangTab lang="python">

```python
# Python code block in a LangTab
card.save("/tmp/my-card")
```

</LangTab>
<LangTab lang="rust">

```rust
// Rust code block in a LangTab
card.save("/tmp/my-card").await?;
```

</LangTab>
</LangTabs>

## Fenced code with copy button

The copy button appears on hover (bottom right) on every fenced block:

```bash
wyrd card register ./my-card/
```

```json
{
  "apiVersion": "wyrd/v1",
  "kind": "Data",
  "metadata": { "name": "example" }
}
```

